# The ShellCheck this repo's gate runs — in CI and in a local sweep alike. `bin/_shellcheck-pinned`
# is the only reader; `.github/workflows/ci.yml` calls that wrapper instead of a bare `shellcheck`,
# so this file is the ONE place the analyser version is written down.
#
# WHY A PIN AT ALL (card#6619). The gate used to run whatever `ubuntu-latest` had preinstalled and
# never named it, so the verdict came from a program neither the log nor the repo identified, and
# the runner image moves with no change here. The two analysers involved genuinely disagree at
# ERROR severity — measured 2026-08-21 on this box, same file, same flags:
#
#     helper() { echo one; }; helper; unset -f helper; helper() { echo two; }; helper
#     0.9.0  -> error: This function is only defined later. Move the definition up. [SC2218]
#     0.11.0 -> clean
#
# So the drift runs in both directions: findings can appear that the current gate does not raise,
# and findings the project gates on today can stop being reported with nothing announcing it.
#
# WHY 0.9.0. It is what the gate was ALREADY running: ubuntu-24.04 image `20260816.277` — the image
# the last `dev` CI run used — ships `shellcheck 0.9.0-1`. Pinning it writes today's observed
# behaviour down rather than changing it. Verified the same day over the gate's own file population
# at `-S error`: 0.9.0 and 0.11.0 both report ZERO findings, over the gate's population before and
# after this change. The pin moves no verdict here either.
#
# NO FILE COUNT IS WRITTEN HERE, deliberately. An earlier revision carried one and it had already
# been hand-re-synced once by the time this shipped — the population grows with every new bin or
# selftest, so a number here is stale on arrival. Re-derive it from ci.yml's own expression if you
# need it; do not restate it.
#
# TO MOVE THE PIN: run the gate under the new version FIRST and diff the findings against the old
# one. A diff is a change to what CI accepts and needs the decision that goes with it — it is not a
# version bump. Nothing tracks this file automatically (Dependabot does not know it exists).
#
# The `asset` lines carry the sha256 of the upstream release tarball for one `<os>.<arch>`, used
# only when the wrapper has to download the pinned build. A platform with no line here is REFUSED,
# never guessed. PROVENANCE: recorded from the artifact fetched on 2026-08-21 from
# https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/releases/download/v0.9.0/ — upstream publishes no checksum
# file, so this pins the artifact AS FETCHED (it detects a later substitution); it is not an
# upstream-attested digest, and it is not claimed to be one.

